# Repairs a SPLIT PACKAGE in the b1.7.3 mappings, which crashes the game on every launch after the
# first.
#
# b1.7.3 bundles the argo JSON library, and FOURTEEN of argo's own helper classes are left unmapped
# in net.minecraft.unmapped instead of being placed back in argo.jdom. argo is written the way a
# small library is -- most of its classes and half its members are package-private -- which is legal
# from inside argo.jdom and an IllegalAccessError from anywhere else:
#
#   IllegalAccessError: failed to access class argo.jdom.JsonFieldBuilder
#     from class net.minecraft.unmapped.C_35499707
#     at net.minecraft.stat.PlayerStats.deserialize -> StatsSyncer.loadStats -> Minecraft.init
#
# It only fires when there is a stats file to PARSE, which is why an instance starts once and then
# never again: the first run writes stats/stats_player_unsent.dat on exit and the second dies reading
# it. Nothing to do with this mod -- it is reproducible on a bare b1.7.3 Ornithe setup -- but it
# makes the game unlaunchable, so it is repaired here.
#
# The list below is GENERATED: every non-public class, method and field in argo.**, which is exactly
# the set a split package can put out of reach. Widening only ever adds access, so the blunt version
# is also the safe one, and it cannot go stale against whichever helper the next code path reaches
# for. The real fix belongs in the mappings, where these classes should be argo's.
